  "overview": "This corpus formalizes a finite counterexample to the proposed 4/3 pairwise-independent correlation-gap bound. It defines the unrestricted and pairwise-moment feasible domains for distributions over subsets, specializes to a five-element four-feature coverage function with rational marginals, gives a three-point unrestricted optimum witness of value 4, and supplies an exact 32-row rational dual certificate proving the pairwise feasible expected-coverage upper bound 479/160. The Lean target packages monotonicity, submodularity, the unrestricted optimum, pairwise feasibility/nonemptiness and upper bound, and the strict ratio comparison; as supplied in the source it contains a proof placeholder, while the run objective requires a proved native formalization.",
  "root_block_id": "root",
